          "name": "Out-of-bounds Write"
        },
        "discovery_date": "2026-04-23T05:01:20.381118+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2461068"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Libgcrypt. During Dilithium signing operations, the library fails to perform a bounds check when writing to a static array. While the data involved is not directly controlled by an attacker, this vulnerability could lead to memory corruption, potentially resulting in a denial of service (DoS) or affecting data integrity.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "Libgcrypt: Libgcrypt: Denial of Service or data integrity issues from missing bounds check during Dilithium signing.",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
